  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q24-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "24",
    "prompt": "$h(x)=\\frac{2x+1}{x-1}$. Find an expression for $h^{-1}(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$h^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-2}$, $x\\ne2$. Interchange $x$ and $y$ and collect the terms containing $y$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{2x+1}{x-1}\\\\x&=\\frac{2y+1}{y-1}\\\\x(y-1)&=2y+1\\\\xy-x&=2y+1\\\\xy-2y&=x+1\\\\y(x-2)&=x+1\\\\y&=\\frac{x+1}{x-2}\\\\h^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{x+1}{x-2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe inverse has domain $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{2\\}$ and range $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{1\\}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
